NNAAMMEE
       pppstats - print PPP statistics

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
       ppppppssttaattss  [ --aa ] [ --dd ] [ --vv ] [ --rr ] [ --zz ] [ --cc _<_c_o_u_n_t_> ] [ --ww _<_s_e_c_s_>
       ] [ _i_n_t_e_r_f_a_c_e ]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       The ppppppssttaattss utility reports PPP-related statistics at  regular  inter‐
       vals for the specified PPP interface.  If the interface is unspecified,
       it  will default to ppp0.  The display is split horizontally into input
       and output sections containing columns  of  statistics  describing  the
       properties and volume of packets received and transmitted by the inter‐
       face.

       The options are as follows:

       --aa     Display  absolute  values rather than deltas.  With this option,
              all reports show statistics for the time since the link was ini‐
              tiated.  Without this option, the second and subsequent  reports
              show statistics for the time since the last report.

       --dd     Show data rate (kB/s) instead of bytes.

       --cc _c_o_u_n_t
              Repeat  the  display  _c_o_u_n_t times.  If this option is not speci‐
              fied, the default repeat count is 1 if  the  --ww  option  is  not
              specified, otherwise infinity.

       --rr     Display  additional statistics summarizing the compression ratio
              achieved by the packet compression algorithm in use.

       --vv     Display additional statistics relating to the performance of the
              Van Jacobson TCP header compression algorithm.

       --ww _w_a_i_t
              Pause _w_a_i_t seconds between each display.  If this option is  not
              specified, the default interval is 5 seconds.

       --zz     Instead  of the standard display, show statistics indicating the
              performance of the packet compression algorithm in use.

       The following fields are printed on the input side when the  --zz  option
       is not used:

       IINN     The total number of bytes received by this interface.

       PPAACCKK   The total number of packets received by this interface.

       VVJJCCOOMMPP The number of header‐compressed TCP packets received by this in‐
              terface.

       VVJJUUNNCC  The  number  of header‐uncompressed TCP packets received by this
              interface.  Not reported when the --rr option is specified.

       VVJJEERRRR  The number of corrupted or bogus header‐compressed  TCP  packets
              received  by this interface.  Not reported when the --rr option is
              specified.

       VVJJTTOOSSSS The number of VJ header‐compressed TCP packets dropped on recep‐
              tion by this interface because of preceding  errors.   Only  re‐
              ported when the --vv option is specified.

       NNOONN‐‐VVJJ The  total number of non‐TCP packets received by this interface.
              Only reported when the --vv option is specified.

       RRAATTIIOO  The compression ratio  achieved  for  received  packets  by  the
              packet  compression  scheme  in use, defined as the uncompressed
              size divided by the compressed size.  Only reported when the  --rr
              option is specified.

       UUBBYYTTEE  The  total number of bytes received, after decompression of com‐
              pressed packets.  Only reported when the --rr option is specified.

       The following fields are printed on the output side:

       OOUUTT    The total number of bytes transmitted from this interface.

       PPAACCKK   The total number of packets transmitted from this interface.

       VVJJCCOOMMPP The number of TCP packets transmitted from this  interface  with
              VJ‐compressed TCP headers.

       VVJJUUNNCC  The  number  of TCP packets transmitted from this interface with
              VJ‐uncompressed TCP headers.  Not reported when the --rr option is
              specified.

       NNOONN‐‐VVJJ The total number of non‐TCP packets transmitted from this inter‐
              face.  Not reported when the --rr option is specified.

       VVJJSSRRCCHH The number of searches for the cached  header  entry  for  a  VJ
              header  compressed TCP packet.  Only reported when the --vv option
              is specified.

       VVJJMMIISSSS The number of failed searches for the cached header entry for  a
              VJ  header compressed TCP packet.  Only reported when the --vv op‐
              tion is specified.

       RRAATTIIOO  The compression ratio achieved for transmitted  packets  by  the
              packet  compression  scheme  in  use, defined as the size before
              compression divided by the compressed size.  Only reported  when
              the --rr option is specified.

       UUBBYYTTEE  The  total number of bytes to be transmitted, before packet com‐
              pression is applied.  Only reported when the --rr option is speci‐
              fied.

       When the --zz option is specified, ppppppssttaattss instead displays the  follow‐
       ing  fields,  relating to the packet compression algorithm currently in
       use.  If packet compression is not in use, these fields will  all  dis‐
       play zeroes.  The fields displayed on the input side are:

       CCOOMMPPRREESSSSEEDD BBYYTTEE
              The number of bytes of compressed packets received.

       CCOOMMPPRREESSSSEEDD PPAACCKK
              The number of compressed packets received.

       IINNCCOOMMPPRREESSSSIIBBLLEE BBYYTTEE
              The  number  of  bytes of incompressible packets (that is, those
              which were transmitted in uncompressed form) received.

       IINNCCOOMMPPRREESSSSIIBBLLEE PPAACCKK
              The number of incompressible packets received.

       CCOOMMPP RRAATTIIOO
              The recent compression ratio for incoming  packets,  defined  as
              the  uncompressed size divided by the compressed size (including
              both compressible and incompressible packets).

       The fields displayed on the output side are:

       CCOOMMPPRREESSSSEEDD BBYYTTEE
              The number of bytes of compressed packets transmitted.

       CCOOMMPPRREESSSSEEDD PPAACCKK
              The number of compressed packets transmitted.

       IINNCCOOMMPPRREESSSSIIBBLLEE BBYYTTEE
              The number of bytes of incompressible packets transmitted  (that
              is, those which were transmitted in uncompressed form).

       IINNCCOOMMPPRREESSSSIIBBLLEE PPAACCKK
              The number of incompressible packets transmitted.

       CCOOMMPP RRAATTIIOO
              The recent compression ratio for outgoing packets.

